	)
	(text "Link to the matrix box (D-56, D-62, D-74, D-79, D-80): Cat6 #1 UTP, T568B, + wire first.\nPair 1 = pins 4/5 data to the box, pair 2 = 1/2 PTT (R1 K0), pair 3 = 3/6 SAFE, pair 4 = 7/8 data from the box.\nEach loop: PNP current source from +13V8, 9.5 to 13.2 mA (C-24). Isolation is at the box end only (optos, D-56).\nLoop 1: DATA_TX high (UART idle) = current = box DATA_RX low (inverted UART). MCU off = loop open.\nLoop 2: R1_TX (FT-710 TX GND through the R1 TX sense) switches the source in hardware: PTT to R1 K0 without the MCU.\nLoop 3 SAFE: KILL switch in series (front panel); SW_STOP_N low turns the source off (software stop).\nThe box READY switch closes the loop (D-62). SAFE_LOST high = no loop current (to the SAFE latch).\nLoop 4: the box PC817 switches the current; DATA_RX low = current (inverted UART).\nDrawn with the cable side on the left and the logic side on the right, as the block on the root sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 218.44 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3cc6b498-6f05-50ea-a258-33d4cee43da0")
	)
